#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:1
msgid "Release 1.1 (2012-07-18)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:3
msgid "This release has the following improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:5
msgid ""
"On Linux, when doing a chroot build, Nix now uses various namespace features "
"provided by the Linux kernel to improve build isolation. Namely:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:9
msgid ""
"The private network namespace ensures that builders cannot talk to the "
"outside world (or vice versa): each build only sees a private loopback "
"interface. This also means that two concurrent builds can listen on the same "
"port (e.g. as part of a test) without conflicting with each other."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:15
msgid ""
"The PID namespace causes each build to start as PID 1. Processes outside of "
"the chroot are not visible to those on the inside. On the other hand, "
"processes inside the chroot _are_ visible from the outside (though with "
"different PIDs)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:20
msgid ""
"The IPC namespace prevents the builder from communicating with outside "
"processes using SysV IPC mechanisms (shared memory, message queues, "
"semaphores). It also ensures that all IPC objects are destroyed when the "
"builder exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:25
msgid ""
"The UTS namespace ensures that builders see a hostname of `localhost` rather "
"than the actual hostname."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:28
msgid ""
"The private mount namespace was already used by Nix to ensure that the bind-"
"mounts used to set up the chroot are cleaned up automatically."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:32
msgid ""
"Build logs are now compressed using `bzip2`. The command `nix-"
"store                 -l` decompresses them on the fly. This can be disabled "
"by setting the option `build-compress-log` to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:36
msgid ""
"The creation of build logs in `/nix/var/log/nix/drvs` can be disabled by "
"setting the new option `build-keep-log` to `false`. This is useful, for "
"instance, for Hydra build machines."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:40
msgid ""
"Nix now reserves some space in `/nix/var/nix/db/reserved` to ensure that the "
"garbage collector can run successfully if the disk is full. This is "
"necessary because SQLite transactions fail if the disk is full."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:45
msgid ""
"Added a basic `fetchurl` function. This is not intended to replace the "
"`fetchurl` in Nixpkgs, but is useful for bootstrapping; e.g., it will allow "
"us to get rid of the bootstrap binaries in the Nixpkgs source tree and "
"download them instead. You can use it by doing `import <nix/fetchurl.nix> "
"{ url =                 url; sha256 =                 \"hash\"; }`. (Shea "
"Levy)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:53
msgid "Improved RPM spec file. (Michel Alexandre Salim)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:55
msgid ""
"Support for on-demand socket-based activation in the Nix daemon with "
"`systemd`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:58
msgid "Added a manpage for nix.conf5."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:60
msgid ""
"When using the Nix daemon, the `-s` flag in `nix-env -qa` is now much faster."
msgstr ""
